# Verdify CODEOWNERS (#82)
#
# Required reviewers for the highest-blast-radius surfaces of the k3s migration.
# A CODEOWNERS match makes @jvallery a REQUIRED reviewer on any PR touching the
# matched paths (enforced once branch protection enables "Require review from
# Code Owners" on live/platform-main + main — that toggle is a repo-settings
# step owned by the human coordinator, out of scope for the agent).
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins. Patterns are repo-root-relative.
# Owner handle is the personal account that administers VerdifyConsultancy.

# ─── Production k3s overlay (the instance whose ingestor is the SINGLE live
#     ESP32 writer; VERDIFY_DEVICE_WRITE_ENABLED=1 lives here and only here).
#     Any change to the prod digests / device-egress allow / device-write
#     interlock must be human-reviewed. ───────────────────────────────────────
/deploy/k8s/overlays/prod/   @jvallery

# ─── CI/CD + all GitHub Actions workflows. These build + publish the in-org
#     GHCR images and write digests back to live/platform-main; a bad workflow
#     edit can mis-deploy or break the loop-break guards. SHARED INFRA per
#     CLAUDE.md (changes route through the coordinator). ──────────────────────
/.github/workflows/   @jvallery

# The CODEOWNERS file itself is owned too, so ownership can't be silently
# rewritten in an unreviewed PR.
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @jvallery
